  "brief_md": "# Evidence Brief: P01 — Multiplayer AI-Agent Workspaces\n\n## Idea\nMultiplayer AI-agent workspaces where teammates can jointly watch, redirect, and hand off long-running agent tasks, for engineering, sales, support, and analyst teams.\n\n## Payer\nMost likely payer is an engineering team lead or eng manager, buying per-seat for the whole team. Anchor comparable: Lody charges $8–10/seat/month for the collaboration workspace alone, with zero markup on model/agent usage (https://lody.ai/price/).\n\n## Competitors\nThis is an actively crowded space as of late 2026:\n- **Lody** — Free tier (2 workspaces/200 sessions/3 members) + Plus $8–10/seat/month (https://lody.ai/price/)\n- **Warp (Remote Control / Business)** — Free tier, Build $20/mo, Business $45–50/user/month (https://www.warp.dev/pricing)\n- **Slack Code (Salesforce)** — Free, bundled into every Slack plan (https://www.salesforce.com/ap/news/press-releases/2026/08/25/salesforce-launches-slack-code-to-make-ai-software-development-multiplayer-2/)\n- **AI Sidekicks** — Open source, free, local-first (https://github.com/Sawmonabo/ai-sidekicks)\n- **AgentsRoom** — Credit-based, $20–$200/month (https://agentsroom.dev/alternatives/warp-dev)\n- Also found in research but not fully priced: GitGhost (https://gitghost.ai/), mpai/multiplayer-ai (https://godfaddaai.github.io/multiplayer-ai/)\n\n## Acquisition Channel\n- **Product Hunt launch**: nominally free, but real cost estimated $3,300–$6,000 in founder time at $50/hr (https://uprowshub.com/campaigns/blog/product-hunt-launch-costs)\n- **Google Ads**: average B2B SaaS CPC ~$8.86; devtools-specific cost per SQL ~$650 (https://www.growthspreeofficial.com/blogs/saas-google-ads-benchmarks-2026-cpc-cpl-ctr-conversion-rate-by-vertical)\n\n## Demand Evidence\n- \"What did the agents actually produce last week?\" — an operations lead, unable to get an answer in under five minutes (https://www.agentcenter.cloud/blogs/why-agents-are-invisible-outside-engineering)\n- \"Slack turns rich execution traces into vibes. Vibes are not enough when an agent is editing production content.\" (https://dev.to/lars_winstand/i-learned-the-hard-way-that-slack-is-the-worst-place-to-find-out-your-website-agent-skipped-the-167i)\n\n## Case For\nThe pain is real and well-documented: agent work is described repeatedly as invisible, scattered, and a 'single-player game' that leaves teammates unable to track or steer it. That several independent small teams (Lody, AI Sidekicks, GitGhost, mpai, AgentsRoom) converged on nearly this exact feature set within months, plus a dedicated YC Fall 2026 RFS on the topic, signals strong perceived demand and a buildable surface: presence, live view, redirect, and handoff as a thin layer over existing coding-agent CLIs, not a new agent runtime. Lody's zero-markup, workspace-only pricing model shows a monetizable path a solo builder could replicate in six weeks.\n\n## Case Against\nThe niche is already a land-grab: at least five direct competitors exist, one (Slack Code) ships **free** inside every Slack plan from an incumbent with massive distribution, setting a $0 anchor price for the core feature. Competing products already advertise SOC2 compliance, Zero Data Retention, SSO, and approval-gated dispatch — security and governance depth a solo six-week build is unlikely to match, and which is plausibly the actual purchase driver for teams letting multiple people steer an agent that touches production.\n\n## Open Questions\n1. Will teams pay standalone, or expect this bundled free into tools they already own?\n2. Does demand genuinely extend to sales/support/analyst teams, or is this engineering-only?\n3. What security/governance bar is required before adoption, and is it reachable in six weeks?\n4. Is there still an underserved wedge given how many near-identical products launched in the same window?\n\n## Regulatory Setup\nData handling and security review (SOC2-type attestation, retention policy) are likely ongoing obligations before enterprise engineering teams adopt shared control over agents touching code or production systems; scope a one-time consult to draft a lightweight security/data-retention posture ahead of enterprise pilots (precedent: https://www.warp.dev/pricing).\n\n## Unsourced Claims\n- A thin session-relay + presence/handoff layer is buildable solo in six weeks [unsourced]\n- Sales/support/analyst demand is separately significant from engineering demand [unsourced]\n"
